rule behaalbare_hoogte_subsidie_1 with provenance the model at decision Behaalbare Hoogte Subsidie rule 1:
the behaalbare hoogte subsidie is the bereken basis hoogte subsidie if
    the bereken basis hoogte subsidie <= the bereken beschikbaar subsidie plafond.

rule behaalbare_hoogte_subsidie_2 with provenance the model at decision Behaalbare Hoogte Subsidie rule 2:
the behaalbare hoogte subsidie is the bereken beschikbaar subsidie plafond if
    the bereken basis hoogte subsidie > the bereken beschikbaar subsidie plafond.

rule bereken_basis_hoogte_subsidie_1 with provenance the model at decision Bereken Basis Hoogte Subsidie rule 1:
the bereken basis hoogte subsidie is the subsidie maximum of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij if
    the gemaakte kosten two >= the minimale noodzakelijke kosten of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij / the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij
    and the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij * the gemaakte kosten two > the subsidie maximum of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij.

rule bereken_basis_hoogte_subsidie_2 with provenance the model at decision Bereken Basis Hoogte Subsidie rule 1:
the bereken basis hoogte subsidie is a number N if
    the gemaakte kosten two is a number M
    and the minimale noodzakelijke kosten of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number K
    and the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number P
    and M >= K / P
    and it is not the case that
        the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number Q
        and the gemaakte kosten two is a number R
        and the subsidie maximum of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number S
        and Q * R > S
    and the subsidie minimum of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is N
    and P * M < N.

rule bereken_basis_hoogte_subsidie_3 with provenance the model at decision Bereken Basis Hoogte Subsidie rule 1:
the bereken basis hoogte subsidie is a number N if
    the gemaakte kosten two is a number M
    and the minimale noodzakelijke kosten of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number K
    and the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number P
    and M >= K / P
    and it is not the case that
        the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number Q
        and the gemaakte kosten two is a number R
        and the subsidie maximum of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number S
        and Q * R > S
    and it is not the case that
        the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number T
        and the gemaakte kosten two is a number U
        and the subsidie minimum of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij is a number V
        and T * U < V
    and N = P * M.

rule bereken_basis_hoogte_subsidie_4 with provenance the model at decision Bereken Basis Hoogte Subsidie rule 2:
the bereken basis hoogte subsidie is 0 if
    the gemaakte kosten two < the minimale noodzakelijke kosten of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij / the subsidie percentage of the subsidie constanten thuisbatterij.

